{% doc %}
  One monthly instalment, in cents: price × (1 + extra cost) ÷ months, rounded
  UP to whole pounds so the advertised payment is never below the real one.

  Same steps as the installment spreadsheet: the total and the monthly payment
  are each rounded to the piastre first, so a percentage typed to four decimals
  (valU's 11.3353%) lands on the provider's own quote instead of a pound above.

  Integer maths only. Floating point turned 12,000 × 1.05 ÷ 6 into
  2,100.0000000000005, which rounds up to a pound too many. The JS twin is
  instalmentAmount() in assets/showcase-instalments.js.

  @param {number} price - Price in cents.
  @param {number} months - Number of monthly payments.
  @param {number} [ppm] - Extra cost in millionths of the price (113353 = 11.3353%). Default 0.

  @example
  {% capture amount %}{% render 'showcase-instalment-amount', price: variant.price, months: 6, ppm: 0 %}{% endcapture %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign ppm = ppm | default: 0
  assign total = ppm | plus: 1000000 | times: price | plus: 500000 | divided_by: 1000000
  assign double_months = months | times: 2
  assign monthly = total | times: 2 | plus: months | divided_by: double_months
  assign pounds = monthly | plus: 99 | divided_by: 100
  echo pounds | times: 100
-%}
